  "description": "Michigan's 9th Congressional District covers the eastern Thumb region and portions of northern metro Detroit. Incumbent Republican Lisa McClain, who serves as Chairwoman of the House Republican Conference, is seeking re-election. The Democratic primary on August 4, 2026, will determine whether Ray Pooley advances as the Democratic nominee. Two independent candidates, Jasen Cartwright and Fernando Valdez, are also on the general election ballot. The district has a strong Republican lean, with Cook Political Report and other forecasters rating it as Solid/Safe Republican.",
